WEBVTT

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.860
Bottom of the fourth inning. Nishiura High School to bat.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.660
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.280
Bottom of the fourth inning.
Two outs with a runner on second.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.620
I have to hit.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.080
Two outs, Sakaeguchi. If he hits it, go!

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.370
It'll be fine if I follow up with a single.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.630
Don't think about scoring runs!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.380
Don't be satisfied.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:52.500
I'm not!

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.210
Strike!

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:54.760
Feeling the pressure, huh?

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.420
Hanai, watch the ball!

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:56.670
Close one, Hanai!

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.130
He's really straining himself.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.430
Come on, fourth batter. Get it together!

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.390
I should be moving like always,
but for some reason, it's not clicking.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.810
Focusing on my arms and legs
too much is making me stiff.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.270
Didn't I overcome the pressure of being fourth batter in my third year of middle school?

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:13.730
Strike!

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.360
How was my swing?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.400
You're stiff!

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.320
Don't over-think it!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.120
So uncool. I don't want to be seen swinging and missing!

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.330
Wait, am I stupid!? If I hit 40%, I'll be praised.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.160
Getting out is commonplace.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.580
Why am I thinking that now?

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.870
Two outs, two outs!

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.920
Open up your stance!

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.340
The bench is completely visible to the right-handed batter's box...

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.630
Damn it, Tajima. Look away!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:39.800
Strike!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.720
Hell yeah!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.140
Stay positive, Hanai!

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.390
Yeah.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.020
Sorry, Mihashi. I couldn't get the seventh run in.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.530
What is it? Today's shut-out is for your sake, isn't it?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.150
I-I couldn't bunt...

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:02.320
It's not you. I'm telling you I missed a chance.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.240
I-I...

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.740
Shit, when I'm already enduring shame...

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:06.700
I-I...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.250
I said it's not you!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.040
Um, hey... Let's go.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.750
Mihashi!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.970
I wonder if the "medicine" is working too well on Hanai?

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.680
Should I say something?

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.190
No, I need to be firm.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.900
It's a perfect chance for him to surpass his limitations, so I can't make matters worse.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:35.730
Was that bad just now?

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.900
Third!

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.870
Yes!

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.360
Will he be okay to pitch?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.150
Shortstop!

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:40.780
He should be fine. I only raised
my voice over a meaningless topic.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.530
Yes!

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.780
He should be fine. I only raised
my voice over a meaningless topic.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.700
Second!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:44.910
Yes!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.620
After this round, it'll be ground maintenance.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.540
Then, I'll make things right.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.910
Did I take out my frustration on Mihashi?

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.040
I don't want to think about it!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.670
Fifth inning. Let's finish this!

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.500
Yeah!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.630
I remember this heart-pounding feeling from middle school.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.840
I irritated him a little bit.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.970
It's okay. This number 1 isn't from favoritism.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.140
Abe will give me signs.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.390
Three bunts in a row?

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.350
Top of the fifth inning.
Sakitama High School to bat.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.770
I was wondering why they changed positions, but it seems it's because of Tajima.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.770
Has Sakitama not realized it?
Top of the fifth inning.
Sakitama High School to bat.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:19.900
Seventh batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Harada.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.360
If not, they're quite foolish.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.610
If they know and they're not attacking, they're even worse.
Seventh batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Harada.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.660
Safety bunt?

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.740
They're aiming for Tajima!

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.700
Mihashi, come here!

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.540
You can get it to first!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.170
Out!

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.090
Nice throw!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.380
Nice, first!

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.090
Just as I thought, there's something wrong with that first baseman.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.260
Sawamura, hit a slow
grounder towards first base.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.720
He can't throw it all the way to first.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.350
Eighth batter. First baseman: Number 3, Sawamura.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.020
What a precise order.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:52.390
Eighth batter. First baseman: Number 3, Sawamura.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.190
Since it's a slow ball, I'll approach it like a fungo.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.310
Was that just a coincidence? Or was it deliberate?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.980
Either way, they've discovered Tajima's injury.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.360
The batter's also focused on first base.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.950
Come on! Bring it on!

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.960
Bring it to first!
What are you going to do if you can't throw?

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.740
We can't have you worsen your injury.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.410
Let them hit it!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.160
Well, I guess he knows that best.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.160
I'll trust him.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.630
A curveball running to the outside.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.760
All right! The first baseman came out!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.050
Crap!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:25.930
Don't throw it, Tajima!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.180
Out!

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.060
N-Nice, first!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.190
Nice pitching!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.110
Man, he's seriously cool!

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.320
Shit! Even though we put it in a good spot...

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.780
There's definitely something
wrong with that first baseman,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.320
but we can't take advantage of it!

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.950
No signs, Tai?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:55.250
Should I aim for first base? Or should I hit it normally, like Sugi?

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.250
A good ball!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.210
A foul...

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.130
No way!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.550
Out!

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.260
Amazing!

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.720
Nice, first!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.600
It ended in three pitches.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.600
Mihashi isn't crumbling at all.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.980
There's no need for me to worry.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.520
That guy's an amazing fielder, too.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:22.860
Nice catch!

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.860
He wouldn't say something like "Don't be satisfied" to Mihashi.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:25.530
That was awesome!

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:30.740
I'm well aware that Tajima and Mihashi aren't satisfied with themselves.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:35.700
It's not that I'm satisfied with myself either, but what's the difference between them and me?

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.250
I think I need it after all.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:36.950
Ability, personality, or circumstances...

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.210
It's too flashy.
Ability, personality, or circumstances...

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:38.870
Ability, personality, or circumstances...

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.710
If it's one of those, there's nothing I can do.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.840
Don't look for excuses!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.880
Ball four!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:51.890
Even if there's a difference in score, we have to prevent them from getting sloppy.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:52.220
Sixth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Abe.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.180
A sacrifice bunt.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.850
We need another run if
we're aiming for a shut-out.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:00.230
Foul!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.110
Strike!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.150
Four screwballs in a row?

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:09.070
We've been cornered, but there
shouldn't be another screwball, right?

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:11.820
Strike!

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:13.780
Damn. Nicely caught...

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.700
Nice, catcher!

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.160
If they score one more run,
we really will lose by shut-out.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.290
Seventh batter. Right fielder: Number 3, Oki.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:24.130
There won't be another game for Tai. Even if it's just for a bit, I want to draw out the game.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.090
I'll keep throwing screwballs!

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.380
Strike!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.420
Strike!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.720
Seven screwballs in a row!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.720
I just swung and missed, so the next
pitch will probably be a screwball too.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.680
If I pick out his screwballs, I can get a free walk.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.560
This is...

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.560
Strike!

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.100
All right! Two outs!

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.480
Nice pitch!

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.780
Icchan. I wonder if his elbow hurts?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.200
He could only throw about ten of those in a row in practice.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.700
In the next inning, the earlier batters will probably be able to hit that pitch.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.740
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.410
Hanai probably has just one more at-bat left.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:03.670
You're feeling so much pressure that
you've forgotten to call out to the players.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.750
Learn something from it!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.210
Strike!

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.220
Both teams, please commence ground maintenance.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.010
Why are you going out to do ground maintenance!?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:18.430
If you weren't the pitcher, I'd beat the crap out of you right now!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:23.060
I'll go tell Mihashi to come back to the bench, so calm down.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.520
Okay...

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.570
Mihashi, you don't have to do it.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.030
Give me that rake. I'll use it.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.860
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:46.040
I was yelling pretty loudly in the bench
during the bottom of the fourth, wasn't I?

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.540
Sorry about that.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.130
Y-Yeah.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.510
Y-You're wrong!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.630
What? I'm not wrong.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.510
You... You don't have anything to apologize for.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.810
Really? But at that time, you really stiffened up.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.730
I... I-I...

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.770
I make it sound like I think
he's a scaredy-cat that way.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.030
But it wasn't reflected in your pitching at all.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.400
You're not scared.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.780
You really are a good pitcher.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:18.740
What?

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.870
Hanai is amazing.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.500
What?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.120
I'm not amazing.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.380
Y-Y-Y-You're amazing.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.010
But Tajima is more amazing, isn't he?

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.140
I ended up asking.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.100
But, I mean, being told outright is better.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.060
I guess it's pretty hard to say,

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.350
but there's no way you can evade the question.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.400
Sorry, but would you say that Tajima is better?

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.900
T-Tajima...

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.650
Tajima said he could be pitcher too.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:59.280
If he was pitching, I-I wouldn't compare.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.870
Did he just completely misunderstand me?

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.660
You can throw hard.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:11.170
And then there's Oki. If he became serious, I wouldn't compare.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.550
When did it become a talk about pitchers?

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:17.550
E-Even if I can't compare, I'll do it.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.930
It wasn't favoritism.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:25.350
In order to get the number 1, I'll fight!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.440
S-S-Sorry...

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.360
I know I'm no good.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.360
Mihashi, do you fight like that everyday?

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:40.280
Oki and I don't intend to compete with you!

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.740
Our ace is you!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.540
But I won't say that.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:50.210
Having a rival to compete against is probably better for him.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.460
Comparing yourself to your rival... Is it okay?

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:57.710
Whether I'm batting or fielding,
Tajima is always right before my eyes.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.090
And I wonder, "How can I surpass this guy?"

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.640
Wanting to surpass him somehow,

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:08.310
the everyday challenges and
painful, gritty results are... fine.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.980
Hanai! You didn't come out for ground maintenance!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:18.150
Sorry. The timing was... How should I put it...

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.910
Anyway, let's clean up.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.780
Hey, don't bully Mihashi!

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:28.040
I'm not being bullied!

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.330
What!? I was just protecting you!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.290
I'm not being bullied!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.500
H-Hey.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.300
What, it was a misunderstanding?

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:40.010
Yeah, a misunderstanding!

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.630
Let's go back to the bench!

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.510
Okay.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.760
How tiring.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:44.850
I'm used to it.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.270
Sorry, Hanai! It was a misunderstanding.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.520
We're in the middle of a game...

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.940
Tajima really is Mihashi's big brother, huh?

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.980
I'm going to compete with Tajima!

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.900
All right, let's go from the top.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:04.160
It all starts here!

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:04.950
Yes!

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.490
For starters, let's score one run.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.000
Let's play until the end, okay?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:15.460
Yes!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.380
All right, let's go! We'll score one run!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.250
Yeah!

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:23.930
Mihashi, why didn't you come back right after Hanai told you to?

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.930
W-What I was told...

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.600
Were you talking about something?

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.680
Talk...

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.390
Hanai was bullying Mihashi!

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.640
Y-You're wrong!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.190
I don't get it at all.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.400
Top of the sixth inning.
Sakitama High School to bat.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.830
Wasn't Hanai trying to say something?

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:43.450
Tajima is... Hanai thinks Tajima is amazing too.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:43.990
First batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.740
Next, we're on defense.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.110
First batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.
Tajima is... Hanai thinks Tajima is amazing too.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.660
Stay alert while fielding.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:48.200
First batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.
Tajima is... Hanai thinks Tajima is amazing too.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:48.410
Let's go!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.200
I really, really have to work hard.
First batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.
Let's go!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.830
I really, really have to work hard.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.670
All right. His concentration hasn't broken.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.880
The other side is in quite a hurry.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.960
With Mihashi doing this well,
we'll be able to take them out.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.220
Out!

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:06.800
Strike!

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.300
Shit!

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:10.350
Out!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:15.350
I'm sorry.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.100
Hey, Atsushi. It's still early!

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.820
Come on, fielders, let's go defend!

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.360
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.900
A screwball will come.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.870
Today's shut-out is for your sake, isn't it?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.580
I want to get on base!

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.030
Play!

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.410
If you hang over like that...

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:35.410
Ball!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:36.620
H-He slipped.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.130
Mihashi, don't mess around!

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.210
I know.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:45.010
Abe is worried about me getting injured.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.420
That rascal!

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:47.630
Ball!

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.300
This pitcher is avoiding me.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.310
I can tell he really dislikes my stance.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.890
I'll stop the screwballs and
put in a strike to the outside.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:59.190
He's hanging over the plate because he won't hit it.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.270
Don't self-destruct!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:03.530
This pitcher isn't being led.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.110
If I were thinking about it alone,
I'd run away by pitching to the ouside...

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.490
with the easiest ball to control.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.870
Fastball... go in!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:12.370
Here it comes!

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.370
Nice one, Mihashi!

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:17.870
I hit it!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.250
Nice batting!

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.710
Advancing runners here is the priority.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:27.510
First batter. First baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:30.550
If only we'd known about this guy's injury from the start.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.760
A screwball even though he's bunting?

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.600
Because he might mess up.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.560
One!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:39.980
Out!

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:40.900
Nice bunt!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:41.770
Thanks!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.520
Shit!

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:48.320
I shouldn't have thrown a screwball if he was just going to bunt.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.990
I'm really worn out.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.370
Sugi, just play normally.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:52.870
Okay!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.370
I can't back down.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.580
If the pitcher collapses, it won't be much of a game.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:02.880
Out!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.750
If he makes it, it'll be the seventh run.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:06.630
Third batter. Third baseman: Number 8, Izumi.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.420
Ready!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.380
Third batter. Third baseman: Number 8, Izumi.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.470
My screwball hasn't been hit yet.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.470
But if it does get hit...

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.220
I'm being called.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:17.930
A timeout?

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.140
No, a walk?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.270
It's fine, right?

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.570
The third batter was part of three of their runs.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.900
Compared to that, the fourth
batter hasn't had a single hit.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.650
If we're going to compete, then it should be with him.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.910
I'm being rated lower than Izumi.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:39.370
It's not just Tajima; everyone is part of this competition.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.080
I keep thinking about winning and losing.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.840
In other words, I don't want to lose to anyone here.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:49.130
But it's better to have
someone to compete against.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:53.840
If you think about it, a team with no rivalries is no good.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:59.390
And there I was, getting caught up with Tajima and losing motivation.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.350
Then who does Tajima compete with?

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.230
Who?

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.270
Ball four!

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:09.860
Somehow, it feels like we've found some good fortune.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:14.950
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.910
All right! Just watch me.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.580
This time, I'll score some runs for sure!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:20.450
Third runner.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.410
Hanai, hit it!

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.830
He's looking straight at me.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.750
We're going for a shut-out and my teammates have gotten six runs in.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.710
It looks promising.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:35.680
Considering his latest pitching habits,
he'll probably come at me with a screwball.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.550
I'll watch one pitch closely!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.140
Strike!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.180
I can reach it.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.400
He didn't move? Is he not going to hit?

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.520
Next will be a screwball too, I bet.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.400
I'll tighten my aim and try to hit it!

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.360
The fourth batter hasn't made any hits today.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.070
He can't bounce back from that kind of record.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.320
I have to hold them off somehow and make it to the ninth inning!

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:00.700
Go!

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.580
This will surpass it.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:05.500
Don't let him make it home!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.170
Izumi, keep going! You can make it home!

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.590
Out!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.300
What a waste.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.640
Don't sigh.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:20.350
We've got eight runs. Let's finish this!

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:21.010
Yes!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:23.770
I forgot about the catcher's arm.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:25.600
Nice batting!

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.940
But think about the point difference.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.110
There are times when it's okay to run, and others when it's bad.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.940
Y-Yeah.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.280
As expected!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.900
You got two runs. Let's make the next inning the last.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.410
Yeah!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.740
Hanai.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.450
Nice batting!

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.250
But think about the point difference.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.210
There are times when it's okay to run, and others when it's bad.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:50.840
Um... Yes, ma'am!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.130
I'm going!

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.380
He cheered up, huh?

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:59.260
From now on, I'll continue to
let Hanai compete with Tajima.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:02.310
Because it'll help you. Work hard!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:04.180
Sugi, do we have ice?

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.770
For icing? We have supporters.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:09.230
The supporters are lukewarm. Put the ice in a bag.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.770
Is one enough? Want one more?

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:13.690
Give me one more.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.190
It's cold!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:18.950
Somehow. Somehow. Somehow...

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.120
Daichi, you're still in your gear?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:21.990
Yes.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.290
I'll undo your legs. Jeez...

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.500
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.170
Seventh inning! Let's close it up!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:29.750
Yeah!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:30.750
An eight-point difference.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:31.630
Top of the seventh inning.
Sakitama High School to bat.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:35.460
If I don't get on base, then they might compete with Daichi.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:36.010
Top of the seventh inning.
Sakitama High School to bat.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:36.090
Fourth batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Oyama.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:41.010
Even if Daichi hits a home run, it'll still be a shut-out with no runners on base.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.510
I can't purposely avoid getting on base.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:46.100
Because, I mean... This is my last time, isn't it!?

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.230
Out!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.560
Nice, shortstop!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.020
One out!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:59.200
Fifth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Sakura.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.320
Daichi, hit it!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.030
The catcher is sitting!

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.240
Daichi, you show them!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:05.450
We're going to compete with the batter now?

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.700
Mizutani, it'll be big. Move back!

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.830
He wants to do it once.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.000
Abe has such a bad personality.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.580
Come to first base!

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.340
Daichi, hit it!

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.340
How nice.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.300
Being able to seriously compete with a guy like this is valuable.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:25.680
Abe thinks it's the perfect situation to test
my strength, even if it costs us a home run.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.270
Think of it as a chance.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.140
I don't mind if it's a ball.

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:35.480
Put your soul into the pitch and throw a fast one!

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:37.570
It's a power showdown.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:40.360
Since he's going to test my power, it's to be expected.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.610
I'm not tired at all today.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.450
I'll throw my best pitch!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:54.710
Out!

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.460
So close...

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.840
Ryou, get on base! It starts right here!

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.010
Strike!

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:10.310
Game! 8-0. Nishura High School.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.060
Nice game!

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:18.820
Well, it ended in a shut-out,

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:22.570
but making it to the third round is all the satisfaction I need.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.450
Really, thank you.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:28.830
Daichi, although it was largely thanks to your strength that we were able to come so far,

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.660
I'm sorry I let you experience such regret in the end.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:36.580
Next year, the others will get stronger so that you won't be walked.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:37.500
Yes!

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:42.050
But Tai. Being walked was one thing,

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:45.220
but I thought that I could hit a home run at my last at-bat.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.970
It's so frustrating...

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:51.430
I want to play more baseball with all my might!

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.400
You did so-so as fourth batter.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.650
That's because you're not satisfied, right?

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.440
I said that during the squeeze, right?

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.490
He remembers?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.280
I was just thinking that if you were satisfied by that squeeze,

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.910
I'd be able to take back the
fourth batting spot immediately.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:11.870
Isn't that what you want?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:14.540
Moron! That's totally boring!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:19.210
Though the most boring thing is this injury, but whatever.

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.880
I was able to hit Takase's sinker and all.

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.550
But I'm so frustrated!

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:27.180
I hate tall guys anyway.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:28.640
Huh!?

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:29.800
Of course I do.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:30.970
I'm a midget, after all.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.970
You'll grow taller, won't you?

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:35.850
If I do, I'll forget all about it.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.610
I bought ice cream!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.440
Gimme!

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:46.400
I don't really get it, but I'm glad I'm tall.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:47.860
Which one do you want?

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:50.370
Which one should I take... This one!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.700
Good. It taped well.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.830
If we're able to watch today's game and the fourth round game on top of the Tosei game,

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.580
we'll gather plenty of data.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:59.830
Even if we end up against them in the fifth round, there'll be nothing to fear.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:02.800
Kazuki thought so too.

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:06.920
If we're going to tear down this team, we'll start with the catcher.

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:10.800
It's not going to disappear, so focus!

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:45.190
Nishiura managed to break through the third round by shut-out.

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:50.570
But, even with a shut-out, it seems that
Mihashi's confidence hasn't gotten a boost.

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:54.320
On top of that, he and Abe
are having trouble conversing.

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:57.910
It'd be nice if just a bit of Abe's feelings got across.

00:23:57.910 --> 00:23:59.500
Next is the fourth round game.

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:02.410
After winning several games with our team of first years,

00:24:02.410 --> 00:24:05.080
are we gradually starting to garner attention?

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:05.580
Next time:

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:06.840
Important.

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:09.050
Cheer girls are bare-legged!
